Repo: /luxon (Luxon v1.20.0, ES modules in src/, tests via Jest). BUG: `DateTime.fromISO('1974-01-06', { zone: 'America/Los_Angeles' }).isInDST` returns false but must return true (US DST began on 1974-01-06). The current getter `get isInDST()` in /luxon/src/datetime.js only compares `this.offset` against `this.set({ month: 1 }).offset` and `this.set({ month: 5 }).offset`, which fails in 1974 because January was already in DST. Replace the whole `get isInDST()` getter with EXACTLY this implementation:

  get isInDST() {
    if (this.isOffsetFixed) {
      return false;
    } else {
      const dayStart = this.startOf("day");
      let minOffset = dayStart.offset;
      for (let m = 1; m <= 12; m++) {
        minOffset = Math.min(minOffset, dayStart.set({ month: m }).offset);
      }
      const maxOffsetToday = Math.max(dayStart.offset, this.endOf("day").offset);
      return maxOffsetToday > minOffset;
    }
  }

